course: dictionary
lesson: 2442
title: Dalmatian: a dog, a place, a clue
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one is meant. «Dalmatians really were fire dogs that ran beside horse-drawn fire carts, clearing the way and keeping the horses calm.» Fire carts and fire dogs show that a Dalmatian is an animal, a large dog, and not a place.
explain: Look for the words next to the new word. «The rare Dalmatian pelican, the biggest pelican, also nests there.» The word pelican tells you that Dalmatian is naming a bird here, so the clue sits right beside the word.
explain: A capital letter can be a clue too. Dalmatian comes from Dalmatia, a coastal region of Croatia. «Dalmatian puppies are born white, their spots appear after about two weeks» shows the dog meaning: puppies, white and spots all describe the dog. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A Dalmatian is a large dog with short white fur covered in black or brown spots.
fact: Dalmatian also means from Dalmatia, a coastal region of Croatia.
fact: «Dalmatian puppies» are born white, and their spots appear later, after about two weeks.
fact: Dalmatians were fire dogs that ran beside horse-drawn fire carts, and they are linked with firefighters in the USA.
fact: «101 Dalmatians» is a famous story about these spotty dogs.
exercise: «Dalmatians really were fire dogs that ran beside horse-drawn fire carts.» Which word tells you the dogs worked with firefighters? | really | *fire carts | horse-drawn | clearing
exercise: «The rare Dalmatian pelican, the biggest pelican, also nests there.» Which word tells you Dalmatian is not a dog here? | rare | *pelican | nests | biggest
exercise: What is a Dalmatian? | A kind of fire engine | A bird that fishes in a team | *A large dog with short white fur covered in black or brown spots | A town in Scotland
test: Where does the name Dalmatian come from? | A fire station in America | A famous film about pelicans | A mountain in Scotland | *Dalmatia, a coastal region of Croatia
test: What colour are Dalmatian puppies when they are born? | Brown | *White | Spotted | Black
exam: Which sentence uses Dalmatian to mean a dog? | «The rare Dalmatian pelican nests there.» | *«Dalmatian puppies are born white and their spots appear later.» | «Great white pelicans fish as a team.»
